e handover and translocation during matrix protein transport.\n\n[METHODS]\nTIM23 complexes were affinity-purified from yeast mitochondria in absence or presence of Jac1sfGFP blocking protein. The isolated complexes were treated with 2 mM DSS (three independent experiments) or 10 mM EDC for 3 h on ice, followed by quenching of the reaction with 250 µM glycine pH 8.0 for 30 min. For SDA cross-linking, 2 mM SDA was added to isolated complex for 2 h at 4°C. The cross-linking reaction was quenched with 50 mM Tris-HCl and free SDA was removed by dialysis. Afterwards, the samples were irradiated with UV light (365 nm) for 5 min at 4°C. The samples were precipitated with acetone, resuspended in 4 M urea/50 mM ammonium bicarbonate, reduced with 10 mM dithiothreitol and subsequently alkylated with 40 mM iodoacetamide. Proteins were digested with the endoproteinase trypsin in an enzyme-to-protein ratio of 1:50 (w:w) in the presence of 1 M urea at 37°C overnight. The reaction was terminated with 0.5% trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) (v/v) and peptides were desalted on MicroSpin Columns (Harvard Apparatus). Vacuum-dried peptides were resuspended in 50 µL 30% acetonitrile/0.1% TFA.  DSS and EDC-cross-linked peptides were enriched by peptide size exclusion chromatography (Superdex Peptide 3.2/300 column, GE Healthcare), while basic pH reverse phase chromatography with an xBridge C18 3.5µm 1x150mm column (Waters) was used to fractionate SDA-cross-linked peptides. LC-MS/MS analysis was performed in technical duplicates on a Oribitrap Q Exactive HF (for SDA treated samples), Oribitrap Q Exactive HF-X (for EDC treated samples), Orbitrap Fusion  or Fusion Lumos Tribrid Mass Spectrometer (DSS treated samples) coupled to Dionex UltiMate 3000 UHPLC systems (all Thermo Fisher Scientific) equipped with an in house-packed C18 column (ReproSil-Pur 120 C18-AQ, 1.9 µm pore size, 75 µm inner diameter, 30 cm length, Dr. Maisch GmbH). MS1 full scans were acquired in the orbitrap (OT) with a resolution 